WEBVTT

00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:10.625
[van door opening]

00:00:12.166 --> 00:00:13.250
[sighs]

00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:15.375
[Nick] Huh.

00:00:15.875 --> 00:00:17.583
It's the Zootennial Gala.

00:00:17.666 --> 00:00:18.875
A bunny comes prepared.

00:00:20.208 --> 00:00:21.208
[Judy sighs]

00:00:21.791 --> 00:00:23.291
You know, I used to dream of

00:00:23.375 --> 00:00:24.958
infiltrating a place
like this.

00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:28.583
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:34.833
You know, this is not
your worst idea.

00:00:35.541 --> 00:00:37.458
Wow, that was almost
a compliment.

00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:39.875
Your worst idea is
what you did with your ears.

00:00:39.958 --> 00:00:40.958
[groans]

00:00:41.666 --> 00:00:42.666
All right.

00:00:44.375 --> 00:00:46.375
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

00:00:55.041 --> 00:00:57.375
[announcer]
Welcome to
the Zootennial Gala...

00:00:57.458 --> 00:00:58.291
[grunts]

00:00:58.375 --> 00:01:01.875
...featuring the original
Lynxley Journal.

00:01:01.958 --> 00:01:05.916
Why would a snake wanna steal
some old book anyway?

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.375
[Judy] I don't know.

00:01:07.458 --> 00:01:08.583
[mouse] Yeehaw!

00:01:08.666 --> 00:01:10.416
But no one is gonna steal it,

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.208
because we are here
to protect it.

00:01:15.625 --> 00:01:18.916
[Judy] The journal is in
the reserved section. Okay.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.500
[Nick groans]

00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:21.583
Come on.

00:01:21.666 --> 00:01:22.666
Slow down.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:26.375
You want to fit in?
Commando is not gonna cut it.

00:01:26.458 --> 00:01:28.375
It's not just the clothes,
m'kay?

00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:30.000
It is the vibe.

00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:32.750
Good to see ya.
Hey, real nice humps.

00:01:32.833 --> 00:01:35.875
Oh, is that real mink?
This is real fox. [laughs]

00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:37.791
Get invited to a lot of these?

00:01:37.875 --> 00:01:40.041
Mmm. Invited? No.

00:01:40.125 --> 00:01:42.583
But there's other reasons
to hob knob.

00:01:43.208 --> 00:01:44.333
[gasps, stifles shout]

00:01:44.416 --> 00:01:46.708
Madam, excuse me.
Is this yours?

00:01:46.791 --> 00:01:48.208
Why, yes.

00:01:48.291 --> 00:01:50.958
-Well, allow me.
-[chuckles]

00:01:52.791 --> 00:01:54.375
Clever fox.

00:01:54.458 --> 00:01:55.458
Ooh, there!

00:01:56.375 --> 00:01:58.791
[chuckles] I don't think
it has enough guards.

00:01:59.416 --> 00:02:01.458
I'll get a closer look.
Watch my six.

00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:06.416
[groans]

00:02:07.458 --> 00:02:09.208
[Nick] Uh-oh. Bogo alert.

00:02:09.291 --> 00:02:10.291
Ah.

00:02:10.958 --> 00:02:12.041
[growls]

00:02:18.708 --> 00:02:20.958
ORIGINAL PATENT
Granted To Ebenezer Lynxley

00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:22.875
Hmm.

00:02:22.958 --> 00:02:25.041
Cover's made of metal.

00:02:25.125 --> 00:02:27.666
[Nick on comms]
Gruffalo
Buffalo has joined the mix.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:28.833
Three o'clock.

00:02:37.166 --> 00:02:39.750
-Oh! Excuse me. I am so sorry.
-Oh! Oh, no. Sorry.

00:02:39.833 --> 00:02:41.666
Here, lemme just... Oh, nope.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.708
That belongs to you.
I apologize. [chuckles]

00:02:44.791 --> 00:02:46.375
Oh, gosh. He hates me.

00:02:46.458 --> 00:02:47.291
Here.

00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:48.916
Ah! You're my hero.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.541
Well, just like to be prepared
for any possible scenario.

00:02:52.625 --> 00:02:55.208
Which is not a weird thing
to say at a party.

00:02:55.291 --> 00:02:57.791
Well, I just mopped a spill
with that guy's tail,

00:02:57.875 --> 00:02:59.125
so... [chuckles]

00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:00.208
Paw!

00:03:01.583 --> 00:03:04.500
Uh, Pawbert. I am Pawbert. Hi.

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:06.041
Judy. I'm Judy Hopps.

00:03:06.125 --> 00:03:07.958
Argh! What the pork?

00:03:08.041 --> 00:03:10.041
Well, 'tis nice
to meet you, Judy...

00:03:10.125 --> 00:03:12.583
Wait. Judy Hopps?
The Judy Hopps?

00:03:12.666 --> 00:03:14.375
[laughs] Are you working this?

00:03:14.458 --> 00:03:16.625
I mean, you're clearly
working it. [chuckles]

00:03:16.708 --> 00:03:18.375
But are you actually
working this?

00:03:18.458 --> 00:03:20.666
[chuckles] Uh, no.
I'm actually...

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:21.958
Well, it's just a hunch.

00:03:22.041 --> 00:03:23.458
...protecting that.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.375
Good. I don't think
it has enough guards.

00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:27.291
[both laugh]

00:03:27.375 --> 00:03:28.958
[Nick on comms]
Uh, that was my joke.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:30.583
Yeah, and there's
nothing here.

00:03:30.666 --> 00:03:32.250
Let's call it a night.

00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:33.333
Hopps?

00:03:38.041 --> 00:03:39.500
-[♪ fanfare playing]
-[guests applauding]

00:03:39.583 --> 00:03:40.708
Well, we should...

00:03:40.791 --> 00:03:41.833
It was nice to meet you.

00:03:41.916 --> 00:03:43.375
Yes, and you.

00:03:43.458 --> 00:03:44.666
Uh, bon appétit.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.791
If, at any point tonight,

00:03:46.875 --> 00:03:48.166
you choose to eat,
bon appétit then.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.083
[Cattrick clears throat]

00:03:49.166 --> 00:03:51.250
You're supposed to be
off stage, Pawbert.

00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:53.458
Yeah, get off stage, Pawbert.

00:03:53.541 --> 00:03:54.666
Wait, are you...

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.291
Yeah, I am a Lynxley.

00:03:57.375 --> 00:03:58.875
Or, you know,
I'm trying to be.

00:03:58.958 --> 00:04:00.041
Now, Pawbert.

00:04:00.125 --> 00:04:01.208
Come on, Papi.

00:04:01.291 --> 00:04:02.375
I got you, Pa.
Don't you worry.

00:04:02.458 --> 00:04:03.625
No, I have him. I have him.

00:04:03.708 --> 00:04:06.208
[Winddancer] All right,
let's get this thing started.

00:04:06.291 --> 00:04:07.916
-[chuckling]
-[crowd cheering]

00:04:09.083 --> 00:04:09.916
Huh.

00:04:10.541 --> 00:04:12.750
[Winddancer] Welcome to
the Zootennial Gala.

00:04:12.833 --> 00:04:15.416
Hey, Hopps.
I think I might actually...

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.666
I think I've got something.

00:04:17.291 --> 00:04:19.000
Ah. Look at you all.

00:04:19.083 --> 00:04:21.541
[laughing] Good to see ya.

00:04:21.625 --> 00:04:23.208
It is with great pleasure

00:04:23.291 --> 00:04:25.666
that I introduce the
third-generation visionary...

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:28.083
Carrots, can you hear me?
I have a trail.

00:04:28.166 --> 00:04:29.125
[Winddancer]
...who has continued

00:04:29.208 --> 00:04:30.583
the legacy of our great city,

00:04:30.666 --> 00:04:32.500
Milton Lynxley.

00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:33.916
Thank you.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.333
-Thank you very much.
-Carrots. Carrots.

00:04:35.416 --> 00:04:36.416
[grunts]

00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:38.958
What are you doing here?

00:04:39.041 --> 00:04:40.041
Chief, she was right.

00:04:40.125 --> 00:04:41.250
-You're done.
-Wait. No, no.

00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:42.166
You're both done.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.000
My grandpa had a dream

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:45.875
to build a city
for all animals.

00:04:45.958 --> 00:04:47.125
Nick?

00:04:47.708 --> 00:04:51.791
[Milton Lynxley]
To truly be better together.

00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:52.833
[gasps]

00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:55.625
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

00:05:02.458 --> 00:05:03.916
[high-pitched]
There's a snake!

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.000
Snake, snake, snake!

00:05:05.666 --> 00:05:07.500
[Zebros] Go, bro, go.

00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:09.458
I will remember you, zebra.

00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:10.791
[gasps, whimpers]

